! WP-U1.8 — WindGen DAILY mode: the load shape supplies the WIND SPEED (m/s), not
! a per-unit multiplier (CalcDailyMult). At hour 1 the shape reads 10 m/s, so the
! aerodynamic curve delivers ~1263 kW (uncapped below kWBase=3000). This exercises
! the daily-mode dispatch + shape-as-wind-speed path (distinct from the snapshot
! deck, which uses the default vwind directly).
!
! SINGLE-STEP (n_steps=1) by necessity: dss_capi 0.15.x caches per-element
! `Losses` and the WindGen does NOT invalidate that cache across daily steps (an
! API-level quirk, delta bucket F "cached total losses" — Currents/Powers ARE
! fresh, only el.Losses freezes at the first step). The corpus_live full-model
! compare includes the oracle's cached (frozen) losses, so a multi-step deck
! would diverge on that channel alone. The port computes losses correctly (fresh);
! the bucket-F caching quirk is out of scope, not reproduced. The full 6-point
! wind sweep + cut-in/cut-out is pinned offline by the unit test
! aerodynamic_wind_speed_sweep. oracle capi015.
Clear
New Circuit.wtg_daily basekv=12.47 phases=3 bus1=srcbus
New Loadshape.wind npts=3 interval=1 mult=(10 15 20)
New Line.l1 bus1=srcbus bus2=wbus phases=3 r1=0.1 x1=0.5 length=1
New WindGen.w1 bus1=wbus phases=3 kv=12.47 kW=3000 pf=0.95 conn=wye model=1 daily=wind vwind=12
Set voltagebases=[12.47]
Calcvoltagebases
Set mode=daily stepsize=1h number=1
